 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Eighteen pages, and two ways to talk about oil, gas and coal. Which one survives?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Negotiators at COP thirty-one in Antalya, Turkey, published the first draft of a deal on Monday, Reuters reports. On fossil fuels it offers two options: repeat the twenty twenty-three pledge on transitioning away, or a stronger call to phase them out."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Both options could still be dropped. Chris Bowen, who leads the talks, said the final wording will not look exactly like this. Belgium's climate minister told AFP that some oil and gas producing nations have reservations."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "The draft also calls for tripling adaptation finance to at least one hundred twenty billion dollars a year by twenty thirty-five. An African delegation source told Anadolu that would cover only around thirty percent of what is needed. Talks are set to end Friday."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will the final deal call for a phase-out? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
